MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Rubber grommets and heat shrink tubing feel like useful next supplies because they help protect wiring during the drilling, fastening, and repair work reflected in my recent purchases.",
    "Flap discs fit the finishing step after cutting, while UV glue offers controlled curing for small repairs that my bulk epoxy may be less convenient for."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Another caliper and infrared thermometer offer little immediate value because I already bought tools for those same jobs recently.",
    "The large lag screws assume a heavy wood project I have not indicated, while the M6 screws require an exact thread and length match before they would be useful."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Buying a measuring tool seems to have been treated as a reason to want another similar measuring tool, even though that need is already covered.",
    "My repeated hardware purchases seem to suggest that almost any screws will suit me, but fastener dimensions and the intended job determine whether I can actually use them."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "Supplies that support the next step in my work, such as protecting wires or smoothing cut edges, can be more useful than another tool that repeats a recent purchase.",
    "Interest does not always mean I am ready to buy: I need to check existing screw supplies, cable and grinder compatibility, and which materials an adhesive can bond."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my hands-on repair interests, but sometimes confuse useful complementary supplies with duplicates or hardware that needs a specific project."
}
